      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A strong border is often seen as an expression of national power and sovereignty, but a rigid and heavy-handed approach can actually undermine sovereignty by creating a confrontationist mentality and a perception that the country is trying to force its will on others. This can lead to resentment, mistrust, and even retaliation from neighboring countries, ultimately eroding the ability to cooperate and coordinate on security issues.\n\nA more effective approach might prioritize cooperation and full-fidelity bilateral and multilateral collaboration, recognizing that borders are interchangeable and porous. An effective example is Australia's approach, with many internal degrees of barriers and fencing, but a pragmatic attitude to work well with neighboring Countries to regulate the more stringent issues that do come affect them at the border.",
      "source": "target",
